Hello,

It is difficult to give you any recommendations based on your description without knowing the structure of your data. You can read in FSTAT, Gentix, GenePop, STRUCTURE, and GenAlEx files into poppr and I would recommend reading the data import section of the manual <https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/articles/poppr_manual.html#import-and-data-types-1>. If your data is formatted in another format (e.g. a spreadsheet with one row per individual and one column per locus as demonstrated in the Getting to know adegenet's genind object section of the manual <https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/articles/poppr_manual.html#import-and-data-types-1>, then you will want ot use the df2genind function <https://rdrr.io/cran/adegenet/man/df2genind.html>.

Best,
Zhian

